# Phase 5 Section B: core.autocrlf=true on Windows dev machines (this
# repo's) would otherwise convert docker/entrypoint.sh's line endings to
# CRLF on checkout, which breaks its `#!/bin/sh` shebang inside the Alpine
# container (`/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter`). Force LF for shell scripts
# regardless of the checking-out OS/git config.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Phase 9 (2026-08-23): core.autocrlf=true was rewriting the working copy of
# every source/doc/config file to CRLF on checkout. The blobs are LF and git's
# clean filter reversed it, so `git status` stayed clean -- but any tool that
# compares raw worktree bytes against blob bytes reports the whole tree as
# changed, which is alarming and wastes review time. Pin LF explicitly so the
# working copy matches what is stored.
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
